{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109975","id":2773374380,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6lTlWs","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109975","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109975.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109975.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109975","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109975/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109975/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109975/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b9f4eba17981dee05bf6c993769be3395d279f34","number":109975,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"visionOS XR module","user":{"login":"rsanchezsaez","id":444313,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NDMxMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/444313?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez","html_url":"https://github.com/rsanchezsaez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_PR co-authored by @huisedenanhai and @stuartcarnie_\r\n\r\nDear Godot community,\r\n\r\nThis PR is a followup to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105628 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109974 (I encourage you to read the descriptions of those PR to get the full context of this contribution).\r\n\r\nThis change adds a visionOS XR module to Godot, which allows building immersive experiences on visionOS.\r\n\r\nThis PR builds on top of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109974, so that one should be merged first.\r\n\r\nAs always, we have tried to align with Godot's quality, style, and engine direction, to minimize any disruption coming from these changes. We'll be more than happy to work with the community on iterating this patch.\r\n\r\ncc @BastiaanOlij @stuartcarnie @bruvzg @clayjohn\r\n\r\n## Technical Discussion\r\n\r\nWe have developed and tested these changes using [Xcode 26](https://developer.apple.com/download/applications).\r\n\r\nThe visionOS XR module only supports the Mobile renderer for now, the Forward+ renderer is not supported.\r\n\r\nTo use the visionOS XR module you must set the new `application/app_role` export setting to `Immersive`. You can choose if you want passthrough or not by the new `application/immersion_style` export setting.\r\n\r\nThen, initialize the visionOS XR module in a script:\r\n\r\n```\r\n    var interface = XRServer.find_interface(\"visionOS\")\r\n    if interface and interface.initialize():\r\n        var viewport : Viewport = get_viewport()\r\n        viewport.use_xr = true\r\n        viewport.vrs_mode = Viewport.VRS_XR\r\n        viewport.use_hdr_2d = true\r\n```\r\n\r\nSome implementation details:\r\n- The visionOS platform now has two different execution paths implemented by the `GodotWindowScene` and `CompositorServicesImmersiveSpace` scenes in `app_visionos.swift`. The `application/app_role` export setting controls which scene is used.\r\n- The visionOS XR interface tries to be as close to the OpenXR interface as possible, to keep main renderer code changes to a minimum. It adopts Compositor Services and ARKit APIs, which is how you render Metal content on visionOS.\r\n- We obtain the head pose twice, once in from the main thread in `process()` so the camera and scripts can use it if needed, and another from the render thread in `pre_render()`, which is needed for rendering. The object cannot easily be shared between threads.\r\n- The projection matrices returned by visionOS have an inverse depth correction applied (visionOS uses the [0, 1] z space, but Godot expects the [-1, 1] z space until the rendering step).\r\n- The `rasterizationRateMap` (the structure that supports foveation on visionOS) is provided through the `get_vrs_texture()` function, using the new `XR_VRS_TEXTURE_FORMAT_RASTERIZATION_RATE_MAP` texture type. It's' passed through the renderer when creating passes/subpasses, to be ultimately set by the Metal driver.\r\n- Apple Vision Pro's' minimum supported near plane is `0.1`. The visionOS XR module's `get_projection_for_view()` function will fail with an error message if the camera has a lower `zNear`.\r\n- The Metal driver has a new dummy `SurfaceCompositorServices`, which replaces `SurfaceLayer` when running in immersive mode. The reason for this is that the Compositor Services API needs to do a `cp_drawable_encode_present()` step with the `MTLCommandBuffer` used by the renderer, and this seemed the most natural way of overriding the `present()` call normally done by the Metal driver.\r\n- \r\n## Testing\r\n\r\nWe have been testing this PR in windowed mode with the [Platformer demo project](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/3d/platformer). We have verified the project continues to work on iOS and visionOS, both with the Mobile and Forward+ renderers using the Metal rendering driver.\r\n\r\nI'm also including a [minimum example](https://github.com/rsanchezsaez/godot-demo-projects/tree/apple/visionos-vr-example/xr/visionosxr_scene) of a project rendering an immersive scene on visionOS. Currently the example has no interactivity, but you can move your head and look around the scene.\r\n\r\nIt looks like this:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dcdd8335-8c2b-4627-9d84-3ee8be3f30c9\r\n\r\n## Missing Functionality\r\n\r\n- High quality video captures as detailed [here](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/visionos/capturing-screenshots-and-video-from-your-apple-vision-pro-for-2d-viewing/) are not currently supported. We will submit a followup PR to support this after this one is merged.\r\n- Pinch input, hand tracking and PSVR2 controller support are not part of this PR. Only classic Xbox/PS4/PS5 game controller input is supported.\r\n\r\n## Next steps\r\n\r\nWe have working pinch input, hand tracking, and PSVR2 controller tracking ready. We'll submit these as incremental PRs, to keep isolated functionality in each of the PRs for easier review. Once these areas are done, we believe porting any existing VR games to visionOS could be relatively easy.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097519,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc1MTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:ios","name":"platform:ios","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":865585000,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NjU1ODUwMDA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:xr","name":"topic:xr","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9548448620,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAACOSHDbA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:visionos","name":"platform:visionos","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":1